masthead: |~md
  # Who runs this SQL

  **Every box on this page is a link.** Click one and your editor opens at
  that file and line. Nothing here was typed by hand: `just dl6-doc` runs
  the benchmark, reads `FACTS.json`, and writes this file.

  `grid_10000` · 3,960 edges · **1,069,200 derived rows** · checksum `9d7239568960d6a8`

  | | |
  |---|---|
  | fixpoint | **2315 ms** (461,857 rows/sec) |
  | peak RSS | 726 MB |
  | statements per tick | 17 |
  | measured | v24.15.0 · darwin/arm64 · 2026-08-06T19:09:35.412Z |
  | batches | **split**, so cost lands per statement |
  | baseline | `FACTS.baseline.json`, 2026-08-06T18:55:29.322Z |

  Links use `vscode://`. Set `DL6_DOC_LINKS=file` for the other kind.
~|

chain: "the call chain, driver down to C" {
  style.fill: "#ffffff"
  style.stroke: "#374151"

driver: |~md
  ### 1 · the driver
  `run.ts` reads the edge file and hands every edge to the
  tick loop as ONE arrival batch.

  ```
  TickFold.run(program, seam, [arrivals], 1_000_000)
  ```

  [`v6/labs/exec_shootout/dl6/run.ts:144`](vscode://file/Users/chrishafley/projects/sprefa-lanes/emitrace/v6/labs/exec_shootout/dl6/run.ts:144)
~|
driver.shape: rectangle
driver.class: driver
driver.link: vscode://file/Users/chrishafley/projects/sprefa-lanes/emitrace/v6/labs/exec_shootout/dl6/run.ts:144
driver.tooltip: /Users/chrishafley/projects/sprefa-lanes/emitrace/v6/labs/exec_shootout/dl6/run.ts:144

tickfold: |~md
  ### 2 · the tick loop
  `TickFold.run` drains the batch queue, calling the program's
  own `tick` once per tick and emitting one tick-log line each.

  [`v6/tsv2/runtime/tickLoop.ts:39`](vscode://file/Users/chrishafley/projects/sprefa-lanes/emitrace/v6/tsv2/runtime/tickLoop.ts:39)
~|
tickfold.shape: rectangle
tickfold.class: runtime
tickfold.link: vscode://file/Users/chrishafley/projects/sprefa-lanes/emitrace/v6/tsv2/runtime/tickLoop.ts:39
tickfold.tooltip: /Users/chrishafley/projects/sprefa-lanes/emitrace/v6/tsv2/runtime/tickLoop.ts:39

emitted: |~md
  ### 3 · the COMPILED program
  `.compiled/reachability.ts`, written by the prolog compiler from
  `reachability.dl6`. Its `runIncrementalTick` names the phases:

  ```
  prepareTick -> applyArrivals -> applyLevelsBeforeEdges
    -> applyEdges -> recomputeLevelsAfterEdges
    -> readBoundary -> promoteFrontiers
  ```

  This file is GENERATED. Regenerate it, never edit it.

  [`v6/prolog/compile/scripts/compile_dl6.sh:1`](vscode://file/Users/chrishafley/projects/sprefa-lanes/emitrace/v6/prolog/compile/scripts/compile_dl6.sh:1)
~|
emitted.shape: rectangle
emitted.class: emitted
emitted.link: vscode://file/Users/chrishafley/projects/sprefa-lanes/emitrace/v6/prolog/compile/scripts/compile_dl6.sh:1
emitted.tooltip: /Users/chrishafley/projects/sprefa-lanes/emitrace/v6/prolog/compile/scripts/compile_dl6.sh:1

levels: |~md
  ### 4 · the level phase
  For a head on a CYCLE of the level graph, this calls the refCount
  reconcile once. Everything else stays a single pass.

  [`v6/tsv2/runtime/1_incremental.ts:819`](vscode://file/Users/chrishafley/projects/sprefa-lanes/emitrace/v6/tsv2/runtime/1_incremental.ts:819)
~|
levels.shape: rectangle
levels.class: runtime
levels.link: vscode://file/Users/chrishafley/projects/sprefa-lanes/emitrace/v6/tsv2/runtime/1_incremental.ts:819
levels.tooltip: /Users/chrishafley/projects/sprefa-lanes/emitrace/v6/tsv2/runtime/1_incremental.ts:819

reconcile: |~md
  ### 5 · THE THING THAT RUNS THE SQL
  `reconcileRefCountStatement` takes the emitted `supportSql`
  array, picks which frontier copies this pass wants, and hands
  the whole list to the seam as one atomic batch.

  Nothing here builds SQL. Every string came from the compiler.

  [`v6/tsv2/runtime/1_incremental.ts:536`](vscode://file/Users/chrishafley/projects/sprefa-lanes/emitrace/v6/tsv2/runtime/1_incremental.ts:536)
~|
reconcile.shape: rectangle
reconcile.class: runtime
reconcile.link: vscode://file/Users/chrishafley/projects/sprefa-lanes/emitrace/v6/tsv2/runtime/1_incremental.ts:536
reconcile.tooltip: /Users/chrishafley/projects/sprefa-lanes/emitrace/v6/tsv2/runtime/1_incremental.ts:536

seam: |~md
  ### 6 · the SQL seam
  `SqlRunner.batch` is the only place TypeScript touches the
  database. It wraps `db.batch` in an Observable and counts
  statements. The bench wraps THIS to time each shape.

  [`v6/sprefa-store/js/src/engine/sqlRunner.ts:38`](vscode://file/Users/chrishafley/projects/sprefa-lanes/emitrace/v6/sprefa-store/js/src/engine/sqlRunner.ts:38)
~|
